\label{lemma-lci-properties}
Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a local complete intersection
morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. Then
\begin{enumerate}
\item $f$ is locally of finite presentation,
\item $f$ is pseudo-coherent, and
\item $f$ is perfect.
\end{enumerate}

